            <div xml:id="d721">

                <pb facs="0819" n="726" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg726"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.516/380: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chapin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-07-06T12:00:00-05:00">July 6, 1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>56. My telegram of July 5, 1 p.m.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d721-f1"/> From de la
                    Rue.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Bank officials here have just received word that Council for Foreign 55 [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] Bondholders has not submitted panel and
                        will not meet until next week.</p>
                    <p>All arrangements made here for transfer Monday, July 8. Do you perceive any
                        objection to our going ahead as planned?”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
